Description: Treat aarch64 (and ppc64 in the Fortran jackets) as LP64 everywhere nclong is
 debian/64bit.patch makes nclong an int on __aarch64__ (netcdf.h.in), but the
 matching 64-bit #if lists in putget.c, xdrposix.c and fortran/jackets.c.in
 still name only __x86_64__ (and, in jackets.c.in, not __powerpc64__).  On
 those targets the code passes a 4-byte nclong as an 8-byte long, which current
 compilers reject (-Wincompatible-pointer-types) and which would corrupt
 memory.  Add the missing architectures so every list agrees with netcdf.h.
Author: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Forwarded: no
Last-Updated: 2026-11-28
